# GCC (including GCC 16.2) does not implement Clang's ext_vector_type
# attribute: it warns that the attribute is ignored and then falls back to
# scalar semantics, so a GCC-compiled build of this fixture measures nothing
# about the vector layout/initialization/ABI under test.  GCC is therefore not
# a semantic oracle here; the dedicated runners (check_ext_vector_layout.sh,
# check_ext_vector_abi.sh) exercise both x86-64 and i686 LCCC output directly,
# the latter against Clang as the oracle for this extension.
LCCC_NO_COMPARE=1
